      "Zero heel drop: heel and forefoot sit at the same height, which removes the forward tilt built into almost every conventional shoe",
      "Thin flexible sole, so the foot bends and grips rather than being splinted flat",
      "The maker states they are 60% lighter than conventional shoes — noticeable if you are covering distance on hard floors",
      "Machine washable, which matters more than it sounds for anyone wearing one pair daily",
      "Free size exchanges — the single biggest risk when buying barefoot shoes online is sizing, and this removes it",
      "Looks like an ordinary trainer, not like toe shoes",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Sold only direct from the maker — you won't find these on Amazon, in a shoe shop, or anywhere you can try them on first",
      "If you are coming out of heavily cushioned shoes, expect to build up gradually over a week or two rather than wearing them for a full shift on day one",
    ],
    blurb:
      "The pick we would hand to someone who stands on hard floors all day, or who has been quietly avoiding the stairs. It is the one shoe here designed around the shape of a human foot rather than around a factory last.",
  },
  {
    rank: 2,
    name: "WHITIN Women's Barefoot Shoes W81",
    brand: "WHITIN",
    score: 8.7,
    scoreLabel: "Excellent",
    grade: "B+",
    bestFor: "Best on Amazon for Women",
